       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a typical analgesic dose.\n- **800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a typical anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inpatient use under close supervision.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into several doses.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is intended, and I'll enter the order. If it is intended, please give me the clinical rationale for the note field."
      }
